Sibuna uses two licenses for its first-party code:

1. Engine: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3.
   This covers apps/sibuna, apps/web, apps/wasm-pow, and libs other than
   libs/console and libs/console-protocol, together with build tooling,
   tests, benchmarks and documentation outside the console directories.
   The complete LGPL text and its incorporated GPL terms are in
   LICENSES/LGPL-3.0.txt and LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt.

2. Console: GNU Affero General Public License, version 3.
   This covers apps/console-ui, libs/console and libs/console-protocol.
   The complete terms are in LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt. Distributing the
   interface as WebAssembly does not remove these license requirements.

The default executable includes the console and is distributed as a combined
work under AGPL-3.0, with the engine remaining available separately under
LGPL-3.0. An engine build without the console uses
-Dconsole=false. Corresponding source,
build scripts and pinned dependency declarations accompany every release tag
at https://github.com/insanai/sibuna.

Companies seeking a version under terms other than LGPL or AGPL can contact the
authors, Vikrant Rathore and Ronak Rathore, about alternative licensing.

Third-party code, styles and data retain their original licenses. See NOTICE
and LICENSES/ for their notices and terms. These notices do not relicense
third-party materials.
